    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9e32ad8c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man running outdoors with a mountainous background and a cityscape below. The text overlay reads, 'i just heard my girlfriend is pregnant.' The overall intent of the meme is to humorously convey the man's reaction to the news — likely portraying him as running away or fleeing from the situation, implying shock, disbelief, or avoidance. The visual metaphor of running is juxtaposed with the text to suggest an exaggerated, comedic response to the news of pregnancy. There is no toxicity present in this meme. The humor is situational and does not target any protected group or individual based on race, gender, religion, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic. The meme relies on relatable, non-harmful exaggeration to create a comedic effect, and does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4aa111d4"
      },
